Level Order Traversal (also called Breadth First Traversal) means visiting nodes level by level from left to right.

Traversal order:

First visit root
Then nodes at level 2
Then nodes at level 3
Continue until last level
Example:

Binary Tree:

        1
      /   \
     2     3
    / \   / \
   4   5 6   7

Level Order Traversal:

1 2 3 4 5 6 7
